def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(117, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEWARE" (15:9) — BE CAREFUL NOT TO WITHHOLD MERCY, FOR WHOEVER WITHHOLDS MERCY IS LIKENED TO TRANSGRESSORS AND THROWS OFF THE YOKE OF HEAVEN, AS IT IS SAID "BASE" — WITHOUT A YOKE. The head row of piska 117 ({SP_(117, 1, "שלא", "תמנע", "רחמים")} "not to withhold mercy"; {SP_(117, 1, "בליעל", "בלי", "עול")} "base — without a yoke"): E30 (checked) — THE WORD "BASE" SPLIT INTO TWO WORDS ("without" and "yoke"): the miser a yoke-breaker; 13:14\'s sons of Belial the word\'s other seat in the Torah (asserted: the Torah\'s two); the English\'s note: an interpolation, piska 93:1\'s twin at 13:14. Fresh.')
srow(117, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "BEWARE" — "BEWARE" IS A PROHIBITION; "LEST" IS A PROHIBITION. ({SP_(117, 2, "השמר", "בלא", "תעשה", "פן", "בלא", "תעשה")} "beware is a prohibition, lest is a prohibition"): THE TWO PARTICLES EACH A NEGATIVE COMMAND (piska 70:1\'s rule, the English\'s note) — "beware lest" at its sixth seat of nine in the book (asserted); the chapter\'s one imperative. Fresh.')
srow(117, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST THERE BE A BASE THOUGHT IN YOUR HEART, SAYING" — THIS IS WHAT IS CALLED IDOLATRY: "BASE" IS SAID HERE AND "BASE" IS SAID THERE, "BASE FELLOWS HAVE GONE OUT" (13:14) — AS THE BASE FELLOWS SAID THERE ARE IDOLATRY, SO THE BASE SAID HERE IS IDOLATRY. ({SP_(117, 3, "זה", "שקרוי", "עבודה", "זרה")} "this is what is called idolatry"; {SP_(117, 3, "נאמר", "כאן", "בליעל", "ונאמר", "להלן")} "base is said here and base is said there"): I2 (checked) ON THE TORAH\'S TWO SEATS OF THE WORD — the miser\'s thought weighed as the seduced city\'s sin (the English\'s note Tosefta Peah 4:20). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 13\'s sitting, deu_13_reeh).')
srow(117, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE SEVENTH YEAR, THE YEAR OF RELEASE, DRAWS NEAR" — THIS IS WHAT R. YOSE THE GALILEAN SAID (PISKA 111 ABOVE): IF SEVEN YEARS FOR EACH ONE, HOW DOES IT DRAW NEAR? SAY THEN: SEVEN YEARS FOR THE WHOLE WORLD. ({SP_(117, 4, "היאך", "היא", "קרובה")} "how does it draw near"): 111:8\'s argument at its own verse — the spine cross-refers to itself by name; the ordinal 15:9 [7] the parser\'s row; the one calendar said a third time. Fresh.')
srow(117, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOUR EYE BE EVIL AGAINST YOUR NEEDY BROTHER AND YOU GIVE HIM NOTHING, AND HE CRY AGAINST YOU TO THE LORD" — MIGHT IT BE A COMMANDMENT NOT TO CRY? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND HE CRY". MIGHT IT BE A COMMANDMENT TO CRY? "AND HE SHALL NOT CRY AGAINST YOU" (24:15). MIGHT IT BE SIN IN YOU IF HE CRIED, AND NOT IF HE DID NOT? "AND IT SHALL BE SIN IN YOU" — IN ANY CASE. THEN WHY "AND HE CRY AGAINST YOU TO THE LORD"? I AM QUICKER TO PUNISH ON ACCOUNT OF ONE WHO CRIES THAN OF ONE WHO DOES NOT. ({SP_(117, 5, "יכול", "מצוה", "שלא", "לקרות")} "might it be a commandment not to cry"; {SP_(117, 5, "ממהר", "אני", "לפרע")} "I am quicker to punish"): THE CRY NEITHER COMMANDED NOR FORBIDDEN, THE SIN UNCONDITIONAL, THE CRY A HASTENER — read with 24:15\'s hireling (asserted: "and it be sin in you" three in the book, seven tokens in order with 24:15); 279:4 THE SAME WORDS AT THE HIRELING\'S VERSE (the outside row); NEVER READ AHEAD — 24:15 waits; the English\'s note the Mekhilta\'s twin (neziqin 18, the widow\'s cry). Fresh.')
srow(117, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT IF YOU GAVE ONCE YOU GIVE HIM EVEN A HUNDRED TIMES? THE TEACHING SAYS "GIVE, YOU SHALL GIVE" (15:10). ({SP_(117, 6, "אפלו", "מאה", "פעמים")} "even a hundred times"): THE THIRD DOUBLING READ AS REPETITION WITHOUT LIMIT (116:12\'s twin from "open, you shall open"); Jephthah\'s "give, you shall give" the form\'s other seat (asserted); Bava Metzia 31b the exam\'s seat for the doublings. Fresh.')
srow(117, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO HIM" — BETWEEN YOU AND HIM. FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH SHEKALIM 5:6): THERE WAS A CHAMBER OF THE SILENT IN JERUSALEM. ({SP_(117, 7, "בינך", "לבינו")} "between you and him"; {SP_(117, 7, "לשכת", "חשאים")} "the chamber of the silent"): THE SECRET GIFT — the Temple\'s chamber where the sin-fearing gave and the poor of good family took, unseen (the Mishnah cited in the Hebrew); routed to 13b\'s docket. Fresh.')
srow(117, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"BECAUSE FOR THIS THING" — IF HE SAID HE WOULD GIVE AND GAVE, THEY GIVE HIM THE REWARD OF THE SAYING AND THE REWARD OF THE DEED; SAID HE WOULD GIVE AND HAD NOT THE MEANS — THE SAYING\'S REWARD AS THE DEED\'S; SAID NOTHING BUT TOLD OTHERS "GIVE" — A REWARD FOR THAT, AS IT IS SAID "BECAUSE FOR THIS THING"; NEITHER, BUT COMFORTED HIM WITH GOOD WORDS — WHENCE A REWARD? "BECAUSE FOR THIS THING THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL BLESS YOU IN ALL YOUR WORK". ({SP_(117, 8, "שכר", "אמירה", "ושכר", "מעשה")} "the reward of the saying and the reward of the deed"; {SP_(117, 8, "נוח", "לו", "בדברים", "טובים")} "comforted him with good words"): FOUR GRADES OF THE GIVER, EACH REWARDED — "thing" (דבר "word") read as THE WORD SPOKEN, the blessing on the speech as on the act (the English\'s note Tosefta Peah 4:17); "because for this thing" ONE seat in the Bible (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(118, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE NEEDY SHALL NEVER CEASE FROM THE MIDST OF THE LAND" (15:11), AND THERE IT SAYS "HOWBEIT THERE SHALL BE NO NEEDY AMONG YOU" (15:4) — HOW ARE THESE TWO VERSES UPHELD? WHEN YOU DO THE WILL OF THE PLACE — THE NEEDY ARE AMONG OTHERS; WHEN YOU DO NOT DO THE WILL OF THE PLACE — THE NEEDY ARE AMONG YOU. The head row of piska 118 ({SP_(118, 1, "כיצד", "נתקימו", "שני", "כתובים", "הללו")} "how are these two verses upheld"): 114:1\'s reconciliation at the other verse, IN I13\'s OWN WORDS ("how are the two verses upheld") WITHOUT A THIRD VERSE — the condition does the third verse\'s work (no code claimed); the two piskaot each cite both verses (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(118, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEREFORE I COMMAND YOU, SAYING" — "THEREFORE": FOR THIS REASON. "I COMMAND YOU, SAYING": I GIVE YOU GOOD COUNSEL FOR YOUR OWN GOOD. ({SP_(118, 2, "עצה", "טובה", "אני", "נותן", "לך")} "I give you good counsel"): THE COMMAND SOFTENED TO COUNSEL — "therefore I command you" the book\'s five, twice in this chapter (asserted); Moses\' "I" the store\'s "?" gloss at 15:11 (the display patch at the tail). Fresh.')
srow(118, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"OPEN, YOU SHALL OPEN YOUR HAND TO YOUR BROTHER, TO YOUR POOR AND TO YOUR NEEDY" — WHY ARE ALL OF THEM SAID? THE ONE FIT TO BE GIVEN BREAD — THEY GIVE HIM BREAD; DOUGH — DOUGH; A COIN — A COIN; TO BE FED INTO HIS MOUTH — THEY FEED HIM INTO HIS MOUTH. ({SP_(118, 3, "למה", "נאמרו", "כלם")} "why are all of them said"; {SP_(118, 3, "מאכילים", "אותו", "בתוך", "פיו")} "they feed him into his mouth"): THE THREE NOUNS THREE MEASURES OF NEED — the gift shaped to the taker (the English\'s note Tosefta Peah 4:10); the doubling "open, you shall open" at its second seat (15:8, 15:11 — asserted). Fresh.')
srow(118, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF HE BE SOLD TO YOU" (15:12) — WHENCE THAT WHEN YOU BUY, YOU BUY ONLY A HEBREW SLAVE? THE TEACHING SAYS "IF YOU BUY A HEBREW SLAVE" (EXODUS 21:2). WHENCE THAT WHEN HE IS SOLD, HE IS SOLD ONLY TO YOU? "AND HE BE SOLD TO YOU" (LEVITICUS 25:39). WHENCE THAT WHEN THE COURT SELLS HIM, THEY SELL HIM ONLY TO YOU? "IF HE BE SOLD TO YOU". ({SP_(118, 4, "מנין", "כשאתה", "קונה")} "whence that when you buy"; {SP_(118, 4, "כשבית", "דין", "מוכרים", "אותו")} "when the court sells him"): THE THREE TWIN LAWS EACH GIVEN A CASE — Exodus 21:2 the buyer, Leviticus 25:39 the self-seller, 15:12 THE COURT\'S SALE (the thief sold for his theft, Exodus 22:2 the kin); the passive "be sold" the third law\'s own verb (asserted: the niphal\'s seven in the Torah); the English\'s note Sifra Behar 7:1; the exam: Kiddushin 14b. Fresh.')
srow(118, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR BROTHER, A HEBREW MAN OR A HEBREW WOMAN" — THE HEBREW MAN HAS WHAT THE HEBREW WOMAN HAS NOT, AND THE HEBREW WOMAN WHAT THE HEBREW MAN HAS NOT: THE MAN GOES OUT BY YEARS, BY THE JUBILEE AND BY DEDUCTION OF MONEY, NOT SO THE WOMAN; THE WOMAN GOES OUT BY THE SIGNS, IS NOT SOLD A SECOND TIME, AND IS REDEEMED AGAINST HER WILL, NOT SO THE MAN — THEREFORE BOTH MUST BE SAID. ({SP_(118, 5, "עברי", "יוצא", "בשנים", "וביובל", "ובגרעון", "כסף")} "the Hebrew man goes out by years, by the jubilee and by deduction of money"; {SP_(118, 5, "עבריה", "יוצאה", "בסימנים")} "the Hebrew woman goes out by the signs"): THE TWO NOUNS TWO TABLES OF EXIT — Mishnah Kiddushin 1:2\'s rows (the English\'s note) laid on the verse\'s "or" (Onkelos "a son of Israel or a daughter of Israel", one seat in the book — asserted); the maidservant of Exodus 21:7-11 the woman\'s twin law (no Onkelos row of it in any ledger, asserted); the exam: Mishnah Kiddushin 1:2, Kiddushin 14b-22b. Fresh.')
srow(118, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SHALL SERVE YOU SIX YEARS" — EVEN THE SON. MIGHT IT BE EVEN THE HEIR? THE TEACHING SAYS "SIX YEARS HE SHALL SERVE" (EXODUS 21:2). WHO PROMPTED YOU TO INCLUDE THE SON AND EXCLUDE THE HEIR? I INCLUDE THE SON, WHO STANDS IN HIS FATHER\'S PLACE FOR DESIGNATION AND FOR THE FIELD OF POSSESSION, AND EXCLUDE THE HEIR, WHO DOES NOT STAND IN THE FATHER\'S PLACE FOR DESIGNATION OR FOR THE FIELD OF POSSESSION. ({SP_(118, 6, "אף", "את", "הבן")} "even the son"; {SP_(118, 6, "מי", "לחשך", "להביא", "את", "הבן")} "who prompted you to include the son"): "YOU" READ TO THE MASTER\'S SON, NOT HIS BROTHER — the son inherits the slave\'s years by two features he shares with the father (the maidservant\'s designation, Exodus 21:8-9; the ancestral field, Leviticus 27:16-21 — the kin by name); the English\'s note Mekhilta neziqin 3; the exam: Kiddushin 17b. Fresh.')
srow(118, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'IF HE FLED AND RETURNED, WHENCE THAT HE COMPLETES HIS YEARS? THE TEACHING SAYS "SIX YEARS HE SHALL SERVE". IF HE FELL SICK AND RECOVERED, MIGHT HE REPAY HIM THE WAGE OF HIS IDLENESS? THE TEACHING SAYS "HE SHALL GO OUT FREE FOR NOTHING" (EXODUS 21:2). ({SP_(118, 7, "ברח", "וחזר")} "if he fled and returned"; {SP_(118, 7, "חלה", "ונתרפא")} "if he fell sick and recovered"): TWO EDGE CASES OF THE SIX YEARS FROM THE TWIN LAW\'S TWO CLAUSES — the fugitive\'s years owed, the sick man\'s not (the English\'s note Mekhilta neziqin 2; the exam: Kiddushin 17a); the compile: the term a count of served years with illness inside it. Fresh.')
